OL,3,CMore than 400 World War Two shells
OL,4,Cfound in French village after wildfires
OL,6,FMore than 400 unexploded World War Two
OL,7,Fshells and munitions have been found
OL,8,Fin France after last month's
OL,9,Fwildfires, local authorities have said.
OL,11,FExplosions were heard near the village
OL,12,Fof Le Porge, in the Gironde region, as
OL,13,Fthe fires swept through the southwest
OL,14,Fof the country in July.
OL,16,FIt's thought the heat caused several
OL,17,Fof the buried shells to explode.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G1/5
