OL,3,CMore than 400 World War Two shells
OL,4,Cfound in French village after wildfires
OL,6,FThe shells are both French and German.
OL,8,FDelemotte told French outlet France
OL,9,FInfo authorities do sometimes come
OL,10,Facross similar situations, but said
OL,11,F"it's rare because here they're
OL,12,Fscattered pretty much everywhere".
OL,14,FThe French official said he believed
OL,15,Fthe munitions were from historic
OL,16,Fdemolition pits.
OL,18,FMore than 220,000 people were
OL,19,Fevacuated last month due to the large
OL,20,Fwildfire near Bordeaux, which burned
OL,21,Fan area four times the size of Paris.
OL,1,W~k4~sj5j5~s1G                    G3/5
